Guance.Windows.Native provides the CMake package GuanceWindowsNative:

    find_package(GuanceWindowsNative CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE Guance::WindowsNative)

Mixed Mode reuses an SDK Handle owned by the application. Install the adapter:

    vcpkg install "guance-windows-native[electron-adapter]:x64-windows"

Include guance_sdk.h, start guance_electron_bridge_server_start() with the
existing guance_sdk_handle, and load these public Electron entry points:

    tools/guance-windows-native/electron/main/index.cjs
    tools/guance-windows-native/electron/preload/standalone.cjs
    tools/guance-windows-native/electron/preload/install.cjs

Full Mode lets the Guance Bridge EXE own SDK initialization and shutdown:

    vcpkg install "guance-windows-native[electron-bridge]:x64-windows"

The feature includes electron-adapter and installs the EXE plus its adjacent
runtime under tools/guance-windows-native. Use startFullMode() from the public
Main Process entry point; do not launch private protocol modules directly.

The port supports dynamic x64-windows. Session Replay is experimental, opt-in,
and disabled by default at runtime. The port has no default SQLite dependency.
